---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Obsidixz Commercial"
  description="What Obsidixz Commercial does and does not provide: research scope, service limits, individually agreed projects, your purchasing responsibility and information accuracy."
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Terms of Service</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="max-width:64ch;">
        What you can expect from Obsidixz Commercial, what is expressly excluded, and
        what is agreed separately for each project. Written to be read, not to deter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="wrap prose" style="max-width:880px;">

      <h2>1. What this service is</h2>
      <p>
        Obsidixz Commercial provides structured supplier research and sourcing intelligence —
        principally <strong>Supplier Discovery</strong>: identification of potential suppliers,
        organisation and comparison of publicly available commercial information, and a
        written report covering what the sources show, with sources and dates recorded.
        Projects are fixed-fee and individually tailored.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What is expressly not provided</h2>
      <p>The service does <strong>not</strong> include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Independent supplier verification, factory or facility inspections, audits, or quality assurance of any kind</li>
        <li>Product testing, laboratory analysis or compliance certification — including food-contact, safety or regulatory sign-off</li>
        <li>Acting as your purchasing authority, placing orders, negotiating contracts, or acting as your agent</li>
        <li>Shipping, freight, customs, logistics, warehousing or insurance services</li>
        <li>Escrow, payment protection, trade finance or dispute resolution</li>
        <li>Legal, financial, tax, customs, or regulatory advice of any kind</li>
        <li>Operation of a marketplace, supplier directory, or supplier network</li>
        <li>Guarantees of supplier availability, pricing, lead times, minimum order quantities, replies to enquiries, or quotations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Projects and quotations</h2>
      <p>
        Each engagement is governed by a written proposal agreed before work begins —
        scope, deliverables, fixed fee and indicative timeline. <strong>Project-specific
        written terms take precedence over the general items on this page for that project</strong> — they
        set the scope, deliverables, fee and timeline for the agreed research. They cannot,
        however, turn an excluded service into something we offer: a research agreement
        does not make us a verification, inspection, testing, logistics or payment-protection
        provider, and does not make us your purchasing authority or agent. Some
        matters are deliberately not published as generic terms because they vary by
        project: payment schedules, refund conditions and timelines are all set out in
        your proposal. Likewise, this page does not state governing law or jurisdiction;
        if a project genuinely requires it, it is stated in that project’s written agreement.
      </p>
      <p>
        No retainer, subscription or ongoing obligation is created by an enquiry or by a
        single delivered report.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Your responsibilities as customer</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide an accurate brief and tell us when requirements change</li>
        <li>Verify supplier information independently before contracting, paying or approving production</li>
        <li>Make your own purchasing, legal, financial and compliance decisions</li>
        <li>Ensure you have the right to share any materials you send us, and that they are lawfully used for the agreed purpose</li>
        <li>Treat the report for your own internal evaluation; re-sharing it or the supplier contact details it contains is your call, not ours — we do not attach a contractual redistribution ban you never agreed to</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Accuracy and limits of information</h2>
      <p>
        Reports are built from public commercial information available on the research
        dates stated. That information can be incomplete, outdated, inconsistent or simply
        wrong; suppliers change ownership, capacity and terms without notice. We record
        sources and dates, and we mark gaps we could not close — but we do not and cannot
        warrant that reported information is complete, current or accurate at the moment
        you read it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reports are <strong>information and comparison</strong>, not recommendations to buy,
        endorsements of any supplier, or a warranty of fitness for your purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Supplier communication and RFQ coordination</h2>
      <p>
        If you ask us to contact suppliers on your behalf, this happens only under a
        separate written arrangement, only where it is feasible and lawful, and only after
        you authorise the specific outreach. We never identify you, your business or your
        product designs to a supplier without your explicit instruction. Supplier replies
        and quotations are not guaranteed; where suppliers do not respond, we will report
        that outcome plainly.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Consequences of use</h2>
      <p>
        You remain responsible for all commercial decisions you make on the basis of our
        reports — including contracts, payments, quality approvals and compliance. Our
        role ends at research and honest presentation: reports are information and
        comparison, built from public sources at stated research dates, with gaps marked
        as such. They are not a recommendation to buy, an endorsement of any supplier, or
        a substitute for your own verification before you commit to anything.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Enquiry conduct</h2>
      <p>
        Do not send us unlawful, defamatory or malicious content, or material you have no
        right to share. We may decline enquiries that are unlawful, abusive or outside
        realistic scope, and we will say why.
      </p>

      <h2>9. The business behind the brand</h2>
      <p>
        Obsidixz is an unregistered business brand operated by Richard Oluwadunmininu
        Olasehinde. Obsidixz Commercial is a business expression of the Obsidixz parent
        brand, not a separately incorporated entity, and nothing in these terms creates a
        partnership, agency or employment relationship between you and us, or between you
        and any supplier identified in research.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:obsidixz@outlook.com">obsidixz@outlook.com</a>.
        To start a project: <a href="mailto:obsidixz.commercial@outlook.com">obsidixz.commercial@outlook.com</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">
        Last updated: 9 November 2026 · See also: <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
